WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.315
[MUSIC]

00:00:05.315 --> 00:00:08.130
How do you dream about changing the world?

00:00:10.212 --> 00:00:14.209
Maybe it's by starting a company
that helps women look and

00:00:14.209 --> 00:00:18.542
feel their best,
creating hundreds of jobs and internships.

00:00:20.487 --> 00:00:25.462
Maybe you're successful in manufacturing
first, before you turn to philanthropy,

00:00:25.462 --> 00:00:27.745
changing children's lives forever.

00:00:27.745 --> 00:00:31.316
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; Or

00:00:31.316 --> 00:00:33.752
maybe it's by getting
elected to the West Wing.

00:00:33.752 --> 00:00:37.652
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; Tonight,

00:00:37.652 --> 00:00:42.312
I'd like to suggest a different,
but just as rewarding option.

00:00:42.312 --> 00:00:44.165
Serving in your local government.

00:00:44.165 --> 00:00:50.048
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; Sometimes,

00:00:50.048 --> 00:00:54.980
it feels hard to separate
government from a TV comedy.

00:00:54.980 --> 00:00:57.604
And when you can't take
government seriously,

00:00:57.604 --> 00:00:59.720
it's hard to care about it or value it.

00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:03.940
Early feedback for this talk included,

00:01:05.420 --> 00:01:08.265
could you find a different word for
government?

00:01:08.265 --> 00:01:12.337
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; It turns people off when you

00:01:12.337 --> 00:01:13.425
say it so much.

00:01:13.425 --> 00:01:17.869
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; I haven't found any good synonyms for

00:01:17.869 --> 00:01:18.821
government yet.

00:01:18.821 --> 00:01:23.113
But tonight, I want to make the case
that you should take it seriously,

00:01:23.113 --> 00:01:28.130
and consider getting involved with
your city hall or state capitol.

00:01:28.130 --> 00:01:33.100
Because state and local government
is the most impactful organization

00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:34.515
that you've never cared about.

00:01:34.515 --> 00:01:38.091
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; And all of you smart, talented people

00:01:38.091 --> 00:01:42.685
should care about an organization
that moves billions of dollars and

00:01:42.685 --> 00:01:45.710
affects millions of
lives in our community.

00:01:47.350 --> 00:01:52.510
Right now participation in local
government is low across the board.

00:01:52.510 --> 00:01:57.332
Only 19% of Americans have contacted
a local official in the last year.

00:01:57.332 --> 00:02:01.450
Only 24% have attended
a local public meeting.

00:02:01.450 --> 00:02:04.767
Those rates are even lower
amongst young Americans.

00:02:04.767 --> 00:02:09.044
But when I asked my friends here if
they'd consider getting involved,

00:02:09.044 --> 00:02:13.320
I hear things like, it's not the highest
and best use of their time, or

00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:15.763
that government is slow and efficient.

00:02:15.763 --> 00:02:20.785
There's this perception that your
frustrating experience at the DMV

00:02:20.785 --> 00:02:26.077
would translate into the impact that
you could have by getting involved.

00:02:26.077 --> 00:02:30.891
And I can't promise you that
government offers the autonomy that you

00:02:30.891 --> 00:02:35.880
might have at a starter, or it will
be as first moving as a tech company.

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:41.790
But I also don't think any of us would
like it if our local police force are fire

00:02:41.790 --> 00:02:46.345
appointments started using Move fast and
break things as their motto.

00:02:46.345 --> 00:02:53.009
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; Slowness in government is

00:02:53.009 --> 00:02:58.028
a design feature, it prevents any
one of us from consolidating power,

00:02:58.028 --> 00:03:02.840
and allows all of us to have
a say in how we are governed.

00:03:02.840 --> 00:03:07.160
And I can promise you, that the slowness
that you sometimes see in government

00:03:07.160 --> 00:03:11.900
does not translate into the impact that
you could have by getting involved.

00:03:11.900 --> 00:03:15.990
There are three reasons why,
influence, scale, and talent.

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:18.802
Let's talk about influence.

00:03:18.802 --> 00:03:23.554
Take Cameron Johnson,
who graduated from the JSB in 2008,

00:03:23.554 --> 00:03:29.740
these days Cameron is the director
of product innovation at Netflix.

00:03:29.740 --> 00:03:32.980
He's also the Vice Mayor
of San Carlos California.

00:03:34.060 --> 00:03:38.815
During the day, Cameron works
on video streaming when you turn

00:03:38.815 --> 00:03:42.234
your phone from portrait
to landscape mode.

00:03:42.234 --> 00:03:47.617
At night he goes to Transportation Board
meetings where he decides on policies for

00:03:47.617 --> 00:03:51.049
roads, public transit and
autonomous vehicles for

00:03:51.049 --> 00:03:54.179
the 7 million people who
live in the South Bay.

00:03:55.280 --> 00:04:00.788
Cameron works on your user experience,
on the Netflix app, and on the 101.

00:04:00.788 --> 00:04:04.360
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; I've seen this ability to have

00:04:04.360 --> 00:04:06.930
immediate influence first hand.

00:04:06.930 --> 00:04:11.698
When I was 25 years old, I worked with
the mayor of Salt Lake County on a project

00:04:11.698 --> 00:04:14.918
to help the homeless and
men leaving the county jail.

00:04:14.918 --> 00:04:20.393
At 25, I got to chair committees,
coordinate data sharing agreements,

00:04:20.393 --> 00:04:25.355
and launched an $11 million project
that provided job training,

00:04:25.355 --> 00:04:29.650
rehabilitation services and
housing for over 300 men.

00:04:32.050 --> 00:04:35.999
So, what's the multiplier
effect of that influence?

00:04:35.999 --> 00:04:37.200
Let's talk about scale.

00:04:38.200 --> 00:04:40.896
You could, for example,
go work at the Gates Foundation,

00:04:40.896 --> 00:04:46.700
which just gave $1.7 billion to education,
that's scale, right.

00:04:47.740 --> 00:04:53.282
The man himself, Bill Gates, actually said
it best in his foundation's annual letter.

00:04:53.282 --> 00:04:56.943
While our foundation is
the largest in the world,

00:04:56.943 --> 00:05:00.790
the amount we give is small
compared to government.

00:05:01.880 --> 00:05:07.470
The Gates Foundation total
endowment of $44 billion,

00:05:07.470 --> 00:05:12.990
is less than the $76 billion
that the State of California

00:05:12.990 --> 00:05:15.930
spends on its public
school system in one year.

00:05:17.140 --> 00:05:23.050
And it's not just education, if you care
about healthcare, energy, transportation,

00:05:23.050 --> 00:05:27.700
chances are that the government deploys
far more resources than philanthropy does.

00:05:29.371 --> 00:05:31.670
Lastly, I want to talk about talent.

00:05:32.730 --> 00:05:36.550
There's a term in baseball called,
value over replacement player.

00:05:37.600 --> 00:05:42.667
It argues that a batters value isn't
the absolute number of runs he hits,

00:05:42.667 --> 00:05:47.668
but the runs he hits over the average
player who would've replaced him.

00:05:47.668 --> 00:05:50.290
Think about your own
value over a replacement.

00:05:51.650 --> 00:05:55.980
For example, if you're going into
consulting you'll be joining

00:05:55.980 --> 00:06:00.626
the 985 other GSB graduates since 2003.

00:06:00.626 --> 00:06:02.542
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; So,

00:06:02.542 --> 00:06:06.971
what happens when you leave
being in BCG in a few years?

00:06:06.971 --> 00:06:12.830
They'll likely replace you with
someone 95% as good from HPS.

00:06:12.830 --> 00:06:19.550
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; The same is not true of government.

00:06:19.550 --> 00:06:26.490
Since 2003, only 22 of us or half of 1%
have gone directly in the government.

00:06:27.590 --> 00:06:31.970
Out of over 33,000 alums
in the alumni directory,

00:06:31.970 --> 00:06:35.040
only 88 are involved in state and
local government.

00:06:36.130 --> 00:06:41.560
That means that our cities and states
just don't have that many people who

00:06:41.560 --> 00:06:46.100
think about traffic and
congestion with an operations perspective.

00:06:46.100 --> 00:06:50.083
Or run a local public health campaign
with a marketing background.

00:06:50.083 --> 00:06:54.570
Or even hire key personnel with
recommendations from Joel Peterson.

00:06:56.220 --> 00:06:58.980
Your value over replacement could be high.

00:07:01.000 --> 00:07:05.620
As you leave the GSB, you're looking for
ways to have impact quickly.

00:07:05.620 --> 00:07:11.100
It's why people do search funds, to run an
organization a few years after graduating.

00:07:11.100 --> 00:07:17.093
It's why do people consulting,
to influence large powerful organizations.

00:07:17.093 --> 00:07:21.545
It's why people do private acuity to
deploy large pools of capital to improve

00:07:21.545 --> 00:07:22.580
organizations.

00:07:23.830 --> 00:07:30.669
You can do all three of these things
a mile down the road at City Hall.

00:07:30.669 --> 00:07:35.573
I've spent this whole talk talking
about what you could do for government.

00:07:35.573 --> 00:07:40.540
But in the end, I'd ask that you value
government for what it does for you.

00:07:41.880 --> 00:07:47.910
Local government takes out your trash,
it repairs the roads that you drive on and

00:07:47.910 --> 00:07:50.425
pays the policeman who pulls you over for
speeding.

00:07:50.425 --> 00:07:54.000
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; It likely runs the schools that

00:07:54.000 --> 00:07:58.560
you attended as a child and the schools
that your children will attend.

00:07:58.560 --> 00:08:01.156
It decides whether you
have a composting bin, or

00:08:01.156 --> 00:08:04.650
whether to utilize renewable energy for
millions of residents.

00:08:05.920 --> 00:08:10.170
It runs hospitals, provides healthcare,
and cares for the elderly.

00:08:11.180 --> 00:08:15.820
These essential services aren't
just things that happen to exist

00:08:15.820 --> 00:08:17.340
in our communities.

00:08:17.340 --> 00:08:21.890
They were developed and
they can be improved by you and by me.

00:08:24.013 --> 00:08:30.002
Teddy Roosevelt once said, far and away
the best prize that life has to offer,

00:08:30.002 --> 00:08:33.560
is the chance to work
hard at work worth doing.

00:08:34.740 --> 00:08:39.100
You all have a lot of options
in how you change the world.

00:08:39.100 --> 00:08:44.250
But I hope that you consider
public service, it is hard work,

00:08:44.250 --> 00:08:47.417
but it is work worth doing.

00:08:47.417 --> 00:08:51.581
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]

00:08:51.581 --> 00:08:55.124
[MUSIC]

